# Milestone: M3
# Covers: when the VM-wide step_budget_remaining reaches 0, dispatch_loop
#         exits with the strand still in RUNNING state; urbi_step returns
#         URBI_STEP_RUNNING and the host is expected to call urbi_step again.
#
# blocked: scheduler mid-flight observation is unit-test territory, not a
#          chk-runner gap.  Catching a strand in the budget-exhausted RUNNING
#          state from a golden-diff fixture would require freezing test-only
#          host-observation hooks (an enqueue-without-drive primitive) into the
#          v1.0 embedding API purely so a .chk file can watch scheduler
#          internals — rejected on API-minimalism grounds.  The step-budget
#          exhaustion path is covered by C unit tests with internal access
#          (tests/unit/test_pipe_budget_exhaust.c, test_dispatch_loop.c).
#          Disposition: covered-by-unit-tests; not a chk target.
# matrix-row: scheduler-budget
